{
  "file": "module4",
  "page": 157,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        67.39069366455078,
        78.23609924316406,
        81.83369445800781
      ],
      "text": "•",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        78.23609924316406,
        67.39069366455078,
        464.8279724121094,
        81.83369445800781
      ],
      "text": "if possible, in pregnancy or during breastfeeding (not an absolute contraindication).",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        89.09461212158203,
        527.4353637695312,
        103.53761291503906
      ],
      "text": "Sometimes, the confirmation of isoniazid resistance arrives late (e.g. 5 months into a 2HREZ/4HR",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        102.29462432861328,
        527.5654907226562,
        116.73762512207031
      ],
      "text": "regimen). In such cases, a decision to start 6 months of (H)REZ–levofloxacin depends on the patient’s",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.99905014038086,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        115.49463653564453,
        272.0397033691406,
        129.93763732910156
      ],
      "text": "clinical condition and microbiological status.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        137.19850158691406,
        527.3858032226562,
        151.64149475097656
      ],
      "text": "If levofloxacin cannot be used because of toxicity or resistance, the patient may be given 6(H)REZ",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        150.3986358642578,
        527.4388427734375,
        164.8416290283203
      ],
      "text": "as an alternative. Based on the results of the evidence review for these guidelines, replacement of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        163.59864807128906,
        527.385986328125,
        178.04164123535156
      ],
      "text": "levofloxacin with an injectable agent is NOT advised. The evidence review could not inform on the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        176.79859924316406,
        381.7195129394531,
        191.24159240722656
      ],
      "text": "effect of other second-line TB medicines on treatment effectiveness.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        207.6424102783203,
        183.658935546875,
        223.30239868164062
      ],
      "text": "Addition of isoniazid",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        230.5103302001953,
        527.6094360351562,
        244.9533233642578
      ],
      "text": "There was no clear evidence that the addition of isoniazid affects patients (i.e. adding benefit or",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        243.71034240722656,
        527.4173583984375,
        258.1533508300781
      ],
      "text": "harm). For patient convenience and ease of administration, the four-drug HREZ FDCs  may be used  56",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        256.9102783203125,
        354.63970947265625,
        271.3533020019531
      ],
      "text": "to deliver the Hr-TB treatment regimen alongside levofloxacin.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        278.61431884765625,
        527.3206787109375,
        293.0573425292969
      ],
      "text": "The use of high-dose isoniazid (10–15 mg/kg per day in adults) was not evaluated in this review owing",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.967351913452148,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        291.814208984375,
        527.4213256835938,
        306.2572326660156
      ],
      "text": "to insufficient data. However, the GDG discussed the effect of increasing isoniazid dosing beyond",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        305.0142822265625,
        527.4113159179688,
        319.4573059082031
      ],
      "text": "that provided in weight-banded FDCs, depending on the type of molecular mutations identified. In",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        316.938232421875,
        527.4207763671875,
        332.6572570800781
      ],
      "text": "inh kat vitro evidence suggests that when specific  A mutations are detected (and when  G mutations",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        331.4142150878906,
        527.4246826171875,
        345.85723876953125
      ],
      "text": "are absent), increasing the dose of isoniazid is likely to be effective; thus, additional isoniazid up to",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        343.33831787109375,
        527.422119140625,
        359.0573425292969
      ],
      "text": "kat a maximum dose of 15 mg/kg per day could be considered. In the case of  G mutations, which",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        357.814208984375,
        527.4508666992188,
        372.2572326660156
      ],
      "text": "usually confer a higher level resistance, the use of isoniazid even at a higher dose is less likely to be",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        369.7381896972656,
        141.40367126464844,
        385.45721435546875
      ],
      "text": "(115) effective  . 57",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        401.85809326171875,
        111.67809295654297,
        417.5180969238281
      ],
      "text": "Dosage",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        424.72601318359375,
        527.3927001953125,
        439.1690368652344
      ],
      "text": "Although the IPD analysis did not provide evidence to address the frequency of dosing, it is best",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        436.6501159667969,
        527.4108276367188,
        452.369140625
      ],
      "text": "(27, 93, 116) to avoid intermittent or divided dosing of the 6(H)REZ–levofloxacin regimen  . In the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        451.1260986328125,
        527.4771728515625,
        465.5691223144531
      ],
      "text": "absence of full information about optimal drug doses, a weight-band dosing scheme for levofloxacin",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.99959945678711,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        464.3260192871094,
        156.86708068847656,
        478.76904296875
      ],
      "text": "is recommended. 58",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        495.1698913574219,
        197.2645263671875,
        510.82989501953125
      ],
      "text": "Drug–drug interactions",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        518.0379028320312,
        527.1281127929688,
        532.4808959960938
      ],
      "text": "Levofloxacin may interfere with lamivudine clearance (increasing the levels of lamivudine) but it is not",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.995199203491211,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        529.9617919921875,
        527.4215698242188,
        545.6807861328125
      ],
      "text": "(44) contraindicated with other antiretroviral agents, and no drug dosing adjustments are needed  .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        544.4378662109375,
        527.567138671875,
        558.880859375
      ],
      "text": "Co-administration of levofloxacin with oral divalent cation-containing compounds (e.g. antacids) may",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.985440254211426,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        556.3619384765625,
        527.4382934570312,
        572.0809326171875
      ],
      "text": "(15) impair its absorption and should be avoided  . Restriction of concomitant use of milk products is",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        570.837890625,
        135.74740600585938,
        585.2808837890625
      ],
      "text": "not necessary.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        601.6818237304688,
        299.4793701171875,
        617.3418579101562
      ],
      "text": "Treatment prolongation beyond 6 months",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        624.5496826171875,
        527.4388427734375,
        638.99267578125
      ],
      "text": "Prolonging of treatment beyond 6 months may be considered for patients with extensive disease or",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        637.7496948242188,
        527.6580810546875,
        652.1926879882812
      ],
      "text": "in those slow to convert to smear or culture negative. In the latter, acquisition of additional resistance",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.998600006103516,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        677.0025024414062,
        526.6246337890625,
        690.7064819335938
      ],
      "text": "Although most countries currently procure the four-drug FDC via the Stop TB Partnership’s GDF, in settings where only the three-drug  56",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        689.8025512695312,
        368.5918273925781,
        700.3065185546875
      ],
      "text": "combination FDC (i.e. HRZ) is available, ethambutol has to be administered separately.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        699.0372314453125,
        524.4194946289062,
        712.7412109375
      ],
      "text": "An isolated  kat inh inh G or  A mutation can correspond to variable MIC levels. This implies that  A mutations do not always indicate low- 57",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        710.9091796875,
        526.428955078125,
        722.3411865234375
      ],
      "text": "kat level isoniazid resistance, and that  G mutations are not necessarily correlated with high-level isoniazid resistance. However, the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        720.5091552734375,
        347.4897155761719,
        731.941162109375
      ],
      "text": "(115) presence of both mutations is usually an indication of high-level resistance  .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        730.6718139648438,
        526.5631713867188,
        744.3757934570312
      ],
      "text": "Studies included in this IPD analysis involved the use of regimens containing levofloxacin (usually at a dose of 750–1000 mg/day),  58",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        743.4718017578125,
        526.8263549804688,
        753.9757690429688
      ],
      "text": "moxifloxacin (400 mg/day) or gatifloxacin (400 mg/day), as well as early-generation fluoroquinolones (ciprofloxacin and ofloxacin),",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        753.0718383789062,
        526.5687866210938,
        763.5758056640625
      ],
      "text": "which are no longer recommended for the treatment of DR-TB. Gatifloxacin is currently unavailable in quality-assured formulations,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        762.6718139648438,
        358.0261535644531,
        773.17578125
      ],
      "text": "and ciprofloxacin and ofloxacin are no longer recommended for use in DR-TB care.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        330.23760986328125,
        801.0170288085938,
        556.099609375,
        811.52099609375
      ],
      "text": "Chapter 2 Drug-resistant TB treatment: Recommendations  143",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "heading"
    }
  ]
}